  "projection_boundaries": [
    "Committed Null UnixChild only: original two post-spawn fcntl operations mechanically delegated to UnixChildSetup.initialize(two_original_fds,false,original_child_id); shared auto-reap method replaces byte-equivalent free implementation. All checkpoint/poll/cleanup/retained-leader semantics unchanged.",
    "Frozen UnixControlChannel projection only deletes unconsumed pair methods and Stdio/OwnedFd imports. The C8-consumed from_stream/start_write/poll_write/close/send implementations remain byte-exact; no ChildInputMode fake caller or suppression.",
    "Unconsumed full A control-pair capability is not certified by this projection. Full actual Engine integration must qualify the real unprojected source later.",
    "Frozen LinuxScannerFilter projection deletes only unused legacy pre_exec install and its std::io import. new/program and the actual C8 BPF construction remain byte-exact; the real C child prctl installation is exercised by C8 tests."
  ],
  "native_validation": {
    "linux_x86_64": "pending actual deterministic RED for new18 inventory",
    "linux_aarch64": "pending actual deterministic RED for new18 inventory"
  },
  "build_dependency": "Only cc=1 in isolated Cargo.toml and existing cc package reference in isolated Cargo.lock; no version/package upgrade, no main-tree edits.",
  "limits": [
    "Actual C fixture IMAGE_ID1/2 build and actual 17 parent tests must succeed on each architecture.",
    "Object nm/disassembly evidence is distinct from Rust unit tests and must be preserved.",
    "Ready or startup EOF never permits publication; no SCM or numeric pidfd_open fallback.",
    "Pre-exec handler reset remains separately unqualified by current exec-after SIGUSR1 fixture.",
    "No ELF installation trust, MFD_EXEC namespace policy, parent Engine driver, mobile provider or full PF06 acceptance.",
    "The19 new declarations are isolated lib-test-only mounting. This projection is not a full non-test Engine/source-layout or unprojected A/B integration acceptance.",
    "Outer namespace cleanup receipt is mandatory; direct execution is denied. Protocol status or Cargo session kill alone never proves all physical children exited.",
    "Workflow60min hard termination is infrastructure failure and does not prove finite cleanup. Native outer receipt must show actual original init wait/reap."
  ],
